            stem: "A plaintiff served a notice of deposition on a corporate defendant, naming the corporation as the deponent and describing with reasonable particularity the matters for examination. The corporation produced a lawyer who said she knew nothing about those matters because she was not employed at the time. The corporation took the position that it had no duty to prepare anyone to testify, because a corporation can testify only through a person with personal knowledge.",
